+# TrustMark Learned-Carrier Pilot Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: execute this plan inline with review checkpoints; this campaign explicitly forbids child agents.
+
+**Goal:** Reproduce Adobe TrustMark-Q on the six frozen synthetic PDF sources and measure exact 61-bit recovery, controls, distortion, latency, and memory under a bounded digital transform pilot.
+
+**Architecture:** Render each one-page PDF to a 144-DPI RGB raster, call the pinned official Rust/ONNX TrustMark implementation for encode/decode, and keep issuance/registry logic in Python outside the public watermark decoder. A deterministic runner uses development sources for smoke, validation sources for one global strength choice, then a separately invoked confirmation stage with no retuning.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Adobe TrustMark Rust crate at `2ecb73ad28d1a3f66ac9dc19e1b667711f14314f`, Rust 1.85.0, ONNX Runtime via `ort` 2.0.0-rc.8, TrustMark-Q ONNX models, Python 3.14 shared read-only environment (PyMuPDF 1.28.2, Pillow 12.3.0, NumPy 2.5.3, OpenCV 5.0.0).
+
+**Spec:** `/tmp/sih-robustness-20260916-control/research/robustness_campaign/SPEC.md` and `/tmp/sih-robustness-20260916-control/research/robustness_campaign/LEARNED_BRIEF.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Write only `/tmp/sih-robustness-20260916-learned`; do not touch main, other worktrees, old chats, tags, remotes, or the shared venv.
+- CPU only; two effective CPUs; target RSS <=1.5 GiB; runtime/models/cache <=1.5 GiB; research outputs <=500 MiB.
+- One validated implementation path only: pinned official Rust/ONNX TrustMark-Q, with a narrow tracked CLI strength/thread patch.
+- Preserve the common development/validation/confirmation split and exact source hashes.
+- Freeze all settings before validation; choose strength on validation only; write and commit `selection.json` before confirmation.
+- Never inspect or test `LEGACY_TRIAL_CAPTURE.jpeg`; all transforms in this pilot are digital simulations.
+- Do not make print-camera, collusion-equivalence, cryptographic authorship, human-guilt, or invisibility claims.
+
+---
+
+## File map
+
+- `preregistration.json`: frozen hypotheses, inputs, transforms, gates, messages, metrics, and exclusions.
+- `SOURCE_LICENSE_AUDIT.md`: pinned source/model provenance, MIT attribution, and audited tensor/ECC conventions.
+- `patches/trustmark-cli-strength-threads.patch`: minimal reproducible patch adding explicit CLI strength and two ONNX intra-op threads.
+- `src/messages.py`: deterministic public synthetic issuer messages only.
+- `src/receiver.py`: registry-only exact classification; it does not derive messages.
+- `src/pilot.py`: rendering, transforms, subprocess timing/RSS, metrics, staged experiment, and result serialization.
+- `tests/test_pilot.py`: deterministic messages, split enforcement, transforms, metrics, and classifier tests.
+- `results/`: model/config manifests, smoke/validation/confirmation/control rows, summaries, and command log.
+- `REPORT.md` and `checkpoint.json`: measured interpretation and next action.
+
+### Task 1: Pin and verify the official runtime
+
+**Interfaces:** Consumes the pinned TrustMark checkout and official Q model URLs. Produces a patched `trustmark` CLI plus `results/runtime_manifest.json` and `results/model_manifest.json`.
+
+- [ ] Record the upstream commit, license, model URLs, expected filenames, and the absence/presence of upstream ONNX checksums in `SOURCE_LICENSE_AUDIT.md`.
+- [ ] Install Rust 1.85.0 with the minimal profile into `.runtime/`, apply `patches/trustmark-cli-strength-threads.patch`, and build `rust/target/release/trustmark` with the upstream lockfile.
+- [ ] Download only `encoder_Q.onnx` and `decoder_Q.onnx`; record byte sizes and SHA-256 hashes before any inference.
+- [ ] Run the official encode/decode smoke on `dev_memo` message A at strength 1.0 and require exact 61-bit recovery.
+- [ ] Commit the plan, preregistration, audit, patch, manifests, and smoke log; never commit models, caches, or binaries.
+
+### Task 2: Implement the deterministic staged runner
+
+**Interfaces:** `messages.issue(source_id: str, label: str) -> str`; `receiver.classify(decoded: str | None, expected: str, registry: dict[str, str]) -> str`; `pilot.py {prepare,smoke,validation,confirm,report}`.
+
+- [ ] Write `tests/test_pilot.py` first with exact expected messages, manifest-hash rejection, receiver outcomes (`target`, `other_issued`, `unissued_valid`, `abstain`), deterministic transform dimensions, and PSNR sanity checks.
+- [ ] Run `python -m unittest discover -s research/robustness/learned/tests -v` and confirm the new tests fail because the modules do not exist.
+- [ ] Implement the three focused modules and rerun the same command until all tests pass.
+- [ ] Copy the six small synthetic source PDFs and manifest into `source_pack/`; make `prepare` refuse any hash/split mismatch.
+- [ ] Commit the implementation, tests, copied sources, and passing test log.
+
+### Task 3: Run frozen validation and confirmation
+
+**Interfaces:** Validation produces `results/validation_cases.{json,csv}` and `results/selection.json`; confirmation consumes the exact selection hash and produces `results/confirmation_cases.{json,csv}`.
+
+- [ ] Run both preregistered strengths on both validation sources, both messages, and every transform; retain every decode outcome and quality/timing row.
+- [ ] Run unmarked, other-issued, wrong-source/context, and donor-residual transplantation controls; count any valid but unregistered 61-bit output.
+- [ ] Apply the preregistered gate and tie-break mechanically, write `selection.json`, and commit it before decoding either confirmation source.
+- [ ] Invoke confirmation as a separate command that verifies the committed selection/config hashes and evaluates both held-out sources without tuning.
+- [ ] Run the no-target-bit alignment scan and output-size checks, then commit complete machine-readable results.
+
+### Task 4: Report the bounded result
+
+**Interfaces:** Consumes only frozen result rows. Produces `REPORT.md`, `checkpoint.json`, an actual-size crop panel, and at most two print-ready PDFs if every print gate passed.
+
+- [ ] Summarize exact/wrong/abstain counts by split, strength, transform, source, and message; include controls, unissued-valid counts, PSNR/ink/background metrics, latency, peak RSS, and failures.
+- [ ] Separate measured document results from Adobe FAQ/paper claims and disclose 61 data bits + 35 BCH bits + 4 version bits, raster-only output, public decoding, and no content binding.
+- [ ] Generate fixed 1:1 readability crops. Generate print PDFs only if the frozen validation gate passed; label them as requiring new matched prints.
+- [ ] Run tests, JSON validation, hash checks, repository status, and output/resource-size checks; update `checkpoint.json` and commit the final safe evidence package.
+
+## Self-review
+
+- Spec coverage: staged split, exact messages, controls, transplantation, digital transforms, distortion, text/background quality, runtime/RSS, payload/ECC disclosure, and print stop rule are each mapped above.
+- Placeholder scan: every implementation step is concrete and no per-image decisions remain open.
+- Type consistency: issuance returns 61-bit strings; receiver accepts decoded strings or abstention; validation writes the immutable selection consumed by confirmation.
