+# Running the bounded TrustMark-Q pilot
+
+The tracked experiment expects an untracked branch-local runtime at repository root `.runtime/`. It never installs into the shared NISHAN virtual environment.
+
+## One-time runtime preparation
+
+1. Clone <https://github.com/adobe/trustmark> at `2ecb73ad28d1a3f66ac9dc19e1b667711f14314f` into `.runtime/trustmark-src`.
+2. Install Rust `1.85.0` with the minimal profile using branch-local `RUSTUP_HOME=.runtime/rustup` and `CARGO_HOME=.runtime/cargo`.
+3. Apply `patches/trustmark-cli-strength-threads.patch` to the clean TrustMark checkout.
+4. Download only `encoder_Q.onnx` and `decoder_Q.onnx` from the URLs and verify the exact sizes/SHA-256 values in `SOURCE_LICENSE_AUDIT.md`.
+5. From the upstream `rust/` directory, build with the upstream lockfile, branch-local `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=.runtime/target`, and `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`:
+
+```sh
+rustup run 1.85.0 cargo build --release --locked -p trustmark-cli
+```
+
+The measured local runtime/model/cache footprint after build was about 1.3 GiB, below the preregistered 1.5 GiB limit. Models, toolchains, caches, binaries, and work images are gitignored.
+
+## Frozen stages
+
+Use the repository's read-only shared Python environment; do not install into it:
+
+```sh
+export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
+export OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2 MKL_NUM_THREADS=2 RAYON_NUM_THREADS=2
+export PYTHONPATH="$PWD/prototypes/nishan_pq"
+PY=__PRIVATE_CAPTURE_WORKSPACE__/SIH/.venv/bin/python
+$PY -m unittest discover -s research/robustness/learned/tests -v
+$PY research/robustness/learned/src/pilot.py prepare
+$PY research/robustness/learned/src/pilot.py smoke
+$PY research/robustness/learned/src/pilot.py validation
+```
+
+Review and commit `results/selection.json` before the held-out command. `confirm` refuses an untracked or modified selection file.
+
+```sh
+$PY research/robustness/learned/src/pilot.py confirm
+```
+
+After confirmation, the following commands only complete the development allocation, add an explicit visible label to the already gated candidate, and assemble the report. They do not participate in selection. The label is a local post-embedding pixel edit, so the packaging command refuses to retain the PDF unless the edited PNG and its 144-DPI PDF round-trip still recover the exact frozen message:
+
+```sh
+$PY research/robustness/learned/src/run_development_completeness.py
+$PY research/robustness/learned/src/package_print_candidate.py
+```
+
+The low-level `pilot.py report` stage was run once to assemble the base machine summary. `REPORT.md`, `results/summary.json`, and `checkpoint.json` then received the explicitly documented post-confirmation completeness and PDF-verification findings; rerunning the low-level stage would intentionally replace that audited consolidation with the base view. The observed outputs and exact command order are recorded in `RUN_LOG.md`; do not rerun a stage as an opportunity to tune after unblinding. The final one-page candidate is `results/print_candidate_test_mixed_A_strength_1p0.pdf`, with its exact hash and round-trip decode evidence in `results/print_candidate_verification.json`.
+
+All transforms are digital. The candidate requires a new matching print in a preregistered pack with an unmarked reference and original-profile control. It must not be tested on historical captures or `LEGACY_TRIAL_CAPTURE.jpeg`.
