+# TrustMark source, model, and license audit
+
+Audit date: 16 September 2026. This audit supports one reproduction path only; it is not a general endorsement or novelty claim.
+
+## Selected upstream
+
+- Official repository: <https://github.com/adobe/trustmark>
+- Pinned revision: `2ecb73ad28d1a3f66ac9dc19e1b667711f14314f` (observed upstream description: remove the NumPy `<2.0.0` constraint).
+- Selected implementation: `rust/`, package `trustmark` 0.2.2 and its official `trustmark-cli`, using locked `ort`/`ort-sys` 2.0.0-rc.8.
+- License: the pinned root `LICENSE` is MIT, copyright Adobe 2023. The official root README explicitly says the MIT license covers both repository code and model files downloaded on first use. The tracked patch retains Adobe's notices and changes only CLI exposure/resource settings.
+- Official FAQ: <https://opensource.contentauthenticity.org/docs/durable-cr/tm-faq/>. It describes printing as process-dependent and gives strength 1.5 as an example. That statement is an upstream claim, not a measurement in this pilot.
+
+No StegaStamp mirror, unlicensed print-camera repository, model login, training data, or second inference port is used.
+
+## Official model provenance
+
+The pinned `rust/crates/xtask/src/main.rs` constructs model URLs from the official CAI CDN root and filenames from `rust/src/model.rs`. Only the Q files were downloaded:
+
+| Role | Official URL | Bytes observed by GET and labelled HEAD | SHA-256 observed locally |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| Encoder | <https://cai-watermark.adobe.net/watermarking/trustmark-models/encoder_Q.onnx> | 17,312,208 | `19b3d1b25836130ffd78775a8f61539f993375d1823ef0e59ba5b8dffb4f892d` |
+| Decoder | <https://cai-watermark.adobe.net/watermarking/trustmark-models/decoder_Q.onnx> | 47,401,222 | `ee3268f057c9dabef680e169302f5973d0589feea86189ed229a896cc3aa88df` |
+
+The encoder graph exposes inputs `onnx::Concat_0` and `onnx::Gemm_1`; the decoder graph exposes input `image`, consistent with the official Rust calls. The audited Rust downloader limits each download to 100,000,000 bytes but publishes no checksum. Therefore these SHA-256 values are locally observed reproducibility pins, not upstream-signed checksums. Model binaries remain untracked.
+
+An initial coordinator handoff associated the two sizes with the opposite filenames because parallel HEAD outputs were not labelled. A new labelled HEAD check plus the downloaded graph inputs corrected that metadata error; it is not treated as an upstream model change.
+
+## Audited tensor and image conventions
+
+From pinned `rust/src/lib.rs` and `rust/src/image_processing.rs`:
+
+- Q encode input is RGB float32 NCHW `[1, 3, 256, 256]`, converted from `[0,1]` to `[-1,1]` after bilinear resize.
+- Q decode input is also 256×256 in the Rust implementation. (The pinned Python path uses a different Q decode resize; this pilot does not mix the ports.)
+- Aspect ratios above 2:1 are center-cropped to the shorter-side square before model resize; ordinary A4 pages use the full rectangle, resized to the square tensor.
+- The encoder receives image input `onnx::Concat_0` and bit input `onnx::Gemm_1`, then exposes output `image`.
+- Residual is `(variant multiplier × requested strength) × (model output − normalized input)`, clamped to `[-0.2, 0.2]`, resized to the original raster using a triangle filter, and added to pixels. Q has a strength multiplier of 1.0.
+- The public decoder thresholds each output logit at zero, then runs BCH validation/correction. It returns a corrected data string or `CorruptWatermark`; it does not expose raw logits or pre-ECC bits. Raw BER is therefore reported unavailable.
+
+## Payload and ECC audit
+
+Pinned `rust/src/bits.rs` and the Python `trustmark/datalayer.py` agree on the selected `BCH_5` layout:
+
+- 100 model bits total.
+- 61 data bits.
+- 35 BCH parity bits using polynomial 137 and correction parameter 5.
+- 4 final version bits: two reserved zero bits plus schema bits `01` for BCH_5.
+- The decoder first tries the indicated schema and may try other supported schemas if validation fails. The returned public value is truncated to the corrected data-bit capacity.
+
+This 61-bit public identifier is not equivalent to NISHAN's original 52,500-symbol, five-colluder profile. ECC validity and exact registry lookup are not cryptographic content binding, authorship, integrity, or evidence of human culpability.
+
+## Local patch boundary
+
+`patches/trustmark-cli-strength-threads.patch` is applied to the clean pinned checkout and makes exactly two operational changes:
+
+1. adds `--strength` to the official CLI and passes it unchanged to the existing library call (the upstream CLI otherwise fixes 0.95); and
+2. changes both explicit ONNX intra-op session settings from 8 threads to 2.
+
+It does not alter model weights, tensors, resize behavior, residual math, bit layout, ECC, or decoding. Build jobs are separately capped with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`; inference is also pinned to two allowed CPUs and sets common numeric/Rayon thread variables to 2.
+
+## Unresolved provenance limits
+
+- Adobe distributes the ONNX bodies over HTTPS and states their license in the README, but the audited Rust downloader provides no upstream checksum or signature.
+- The Adobe Stock training-data statement in the FAQ was not independently audited.
+- This pilot reproduces integration behavior only; it does not reproduce training or published paper tables.
